window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b157-3c2e047d5e60cd1d.json"]={sha256:"3c2e047d5e60cd1d8ac7de8f64ca87d8598fffc9310fc8ebc329f759ef9d9b91",value:{"id":"b157","title":"隧道防水膜鋪設","titleEn":"Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以水壓邊界、焊縫與分區連續性驗證隧道防水膜為主線，從水頭與結構承壓邊界與基面平整與膜材跨空建立系統邊界，再把雙焊道試驗與溫度修正、穿透構件與接縫變形連到耐久相容與維護交接。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 十單元以可核算的模型和可追溯證據逐步判讀不同失效。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on verify tunnel membranes through pressure boundaries, seams and compartment continuity. It begins with Head and structural pressure boundary and Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging, links Dual-seam tests and temperature effects and Penetrations and joint movement, and ends with Durability compatibility and handover. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. Ten units use reproducible models and traceable evidence to distinguish failure mechanisms.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-support","subcategoryTitle":"岩體支護與襯砌","subcategoryTitleEn":"Rock support and tunnel linings","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-support","learningTags":["underground","ug-support","support"],"architectureFamily":"support","architectureNodes":[["水頭與結構承壓邊界","Head and structural pressure boundary"],["膜材厚度與批次差異","Membrane thickness and batch differences"],["雙焊道試驗與溫度修正","Dual-seam tests and temperature effects"],["穿透構件與接縫變形","Penetrations and joint movement"],["耐久相容與維護交接","Durability compatibility and handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"support","labels":["水頭與結構承壓邊界","膜材厚度與批次差異","雙焊道試驗與溫度修正","穿透構件與接縫變形","耐久相容與維護交接"],"labelsEn":["Head and structural pressure boundary","Membrane thickness and batch differences","Dual-seam tests and temperature effects","Penetrations and joint movement","Durability compatibility and handover"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例所有輸入均為教學假設。首先檢查水頭與結構承壓邊界：p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa；再獨立檢查基面平整與膜材跨空：localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。水頭由 20 增為 30 m 時，淡水壓力由 196.2 增為 294.3 kPa；膜後排水堵塞的水頭須與結構模型一致。 兩個結果不能自動組成完整設計，因為防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 將將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結作為模型以外的驗證證據，並保留原始紀錄與尚待確認的邊界。","textEn":"All inputs in this integrated example are teaching assumptions. First check Head and structural pressure boundary: p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa. Independently check Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging: localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent. Raising freshwater head from 20 to 30 m increases pressure from 196.2 to 294.3 kPa; a blocked-drain head must agree with the structural model. The two results are not a complete design because the membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. Use link membrane photographs and patch ids to completion of the final crossing trade as evidence independent of the calculation, retaining raw records and unverified boundaries.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b157-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「水頭與結構承壓邊界」與「基面平整與膜材跨空」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Head and structural pressure boundary\" and \"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b157-v14-01","title":"水頭與結構承壓邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Head and structural pressure boundary: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「水頭與結構承壓邊界」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Head and structural pressure boundary” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"防水膜本身不會讓地下水壓消失，封閉系統需要襯砌承受相應壓力，排水系統則依可靠排導降低水頭。將排水型和承壓型細部混用會留下不明荷載；必須明確寫出正常、堵塞和維修狀態的水壓邊界。 判別這個機制時，應觀察對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接；若出現排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水頭與結構承壓邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A membrane does not eliminate groundwater pressure: a closed system transfers pressure to lining, while a drained system relies on discharge to reduce head. Mixing the two concepts leaves undefined loads. Define pressure boundaries for normal operation, blockage and maintenance states. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections. If blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Head and structural pressure boundary” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水頭與結構承壓邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Head and structural pressure boundary”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-01-k1","title":"水頭與結構承壓邊界","titleEn":"Head and structural pressure boundary","text":"防水膜本身不會讓地下水壓消失，封閉系統需要襯砌承受相應壓力，排水系統則依可靠排導降低水頭。將排水型和承壓型細部混用會留下不明荷載；必須明確寫出正常、堵塞和維修狀態的水壓邊界。","textEn":"A membrane does not eliminate groundwater pressure: a closed system transfers pressure to lining, while a drained system relies on discharge to reduce head. Mixing the two concepts leaves undefined loads.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水頭與結構承壓邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Head and structural pressure boundary\" is correct?","options":["只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌","防水膜本身不會讓地下水壓消失，封閉系統需要襯砌承受相應壓力，排水系統則依可靠排導降低水頭。","膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面"],"optionsEn":["A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining","A membrane does not eliminate groundwater pressure: a closed system transfers pressure to lining, while a drained system relies on discharge to reduce head.","High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections"],"answer":1,"explanation":"防水膜本身不會讓地下水壓消失，封閉系統需要襯砌承受相應壓力，排水系統則依可靠排導降低水頭。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A membrane does not eliminate groundwater pressure: a closed system transfers pressure to lining, while a drained system relies on discharge to reduce head. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b157-v14-02","title":"水頭與結構承壓邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Head and structural pressure boundary: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水頭與結構承壓邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Head and structural pressure boundary” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水頭與結構承壓邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Head and structural pressure boundary\", which statement holds?","options":["焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合","圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離","原創教學假設：p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width","Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place","Original teaching assumptions: p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: p=rho*g*h=1000 kg/m3*9.81 m/s2*20 m=196200 Pa=196.2 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b157-v14-03","title":"水頭與結構承壓邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Head and structural pressure boundary: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水頭與結構承壓邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Head and structural pressure boundary” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水頭與結構承壓邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Head and structural pressure boundary\"?","options":["對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面"],"optionsEn":["Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check"],"answer":0,"explanation":"對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b157-v14-04","title":"水頭與結構承壓邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Head and structural pressure boundary: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水頭與結構承壓邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Head and structural pressure boundary” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接；若出現排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照地下水位、膜後水壓及排水通路的實際連接，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare groundwater level, behind-membrane pressure and actual drain connections to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水頭與結構承壓邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Head and structural pressure boundary\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力。","膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption.","High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections"],"answer":1,"explanation":"排水堵塞卻仍沿用低水頭設計，使襯砌承受未檢核壓力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked drains leave lining exposed to pressure omitted by a low-head assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b157-v14-05","title":"基面平整與膜材跨空：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「基面平整與膜材跨空」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"尖突和凹穴使膜材在混凝土擠壓下局部拉伸或刺穿，名義厚度不能補救不相容基面。柔軟墊層分散接觸但也可能壓縮，膜跨越空洞時的拉伸與支承條件不同；基面幾何應在被覆前留下可追溯紀錄。 判別這個機制時，應觀察以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置；若出現膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「基面平整與膜材跨空」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Projections and hollows stretch or puncture membrane under concrete pressure; nominal thickness cannot cure an incompatible substrate. Cushioning spreads contact but can compress, while bridging a cavity changes restraint. Record substrate geometry before it is concealed by the membrane. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates. If concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「基面平整與膜材跨空」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-05-k1","title":"基面平整與膜材跨空","titleEn":"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging","text":"尖突和凹穴使膜材在混凝土擠壓下局部拉伸或刺穿，名義厚度不能補救不相容基面。柔軟墊層分散接觸但也可能壓縮，膜跨越空洞時的拉伸與支承條件不同；基面幾何應在被覆前留下可追溯紀錄。","textEn":"Projections and hollows stretch or puncture membrane under concrete pressure; nominal thickness cannot cure an incompatible substrate. Cushioning spreads contact but can compress, while bridging a cavity changes restraint.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基面平整與膜材跨空」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging\" is correct?","options":["膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面","捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點","尖突和凹穴使膜材在混凝土擠壓下局部拉伸或刺穿，名義厚度不能補救不相容基面。"],"optionsEn":["High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections","Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored","Projections and hollows stretch or puncture membrane under concrete pressure; nominal thickness cannot cure an incompatible substrate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尖突和凹穴使膜材在混凝土擠壓下局部拉伸或刺穿，名義厚度不能補救不相容基面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Projections and hollows stretch or puncture membrane under concrete pressure; nominal thickness cannot cure an incompatible substrate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b157-v14-06","title":"基面平整與膜材跨空：定量估算","titleEn":"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「基面平整與膜材跨空」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基面平整與膜材跨空」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。","任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞","材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent.","Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane","Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: localExtension=(105-100) mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b157-v14-07","title":"基面平整與膜材跨空：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「基面平整與膜材跨空」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基面平整與膜材跨空」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置。","內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates.","An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b157-v14-08","title":"基面平整與膜材跨空：失效診斷","titleEn":"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「基面平整與膜材跨空」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置；若出現膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以輪廓量測與接觸樣板標示尖突、凹穴及墊層位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to map projections, hollows and cushioning using profile measurements and contact templates to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基面平整與膜材跨空」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Substrate smoothness and membrane bridging\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點","膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored","Concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"膜材被混凝土壓入凹穴而局部拉裂，表面原本看似平順。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Concrete pushes membrane into a hollow and tears it despite a previously smooth appearance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b157-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「膜材厚度與批次差異」與「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Membrane thickness and batch differences\" and \"Effective seam width and peeling\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b157-v14-09","title":"膜材厚度與批次差異：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Membrane thickness and batch differences: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「膜材厚度與批次差異」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Membrane thickness and batch differences” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"膜厚是耐穿刺與加工品質的一部分，性能還取決於配方、老化及焊接相容性。局部薄區可能沿捲材邊緣或摺痕出現，平均厚度合格不代表最薄點合格；不同批次材料的接合需證明相容，不能只憑顏色辨認。 判別這個機制時，應觀察分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置；若出現局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「膜材厚度與批次差異」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Thickness contributes to puncture resistance and quality, while formulation, ageing and weld compatibility also matter. Thin zones may occur near edges or folds despite a passing mean. Demonstrate compatibility between batches rather than identifying material from colour alone. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position. If a locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Membrane thickness and batch differences” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80.","failure":"常見誤解：「捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「膜材厚度與批次差異」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Membrane thickness and batch differences”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-09-k1","title":"膜材厚度與批次差異","titleEn":"Membrane thickness and batch differences","text":"膜厚是耐穿刺與加工品質的一部分，性能還取決於配方、老化及焊接相容性。局部薄區可能沿捲材邊緣或摺痕出現，平均厚度合格不代表最薄點合格；不同批次材料的接合需證明相容，不能只憑顏色辨認。","textEn":"Thickness contributes to puncture resistance and quality, while formulation, ageing and weld compatibility also matter. Thin zones may occur near edges or folds despite a passing mean.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「膜材厚度與批次差異」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Membrane thickness and batch differences\" is correct?","options":["膜厚是耐穿刺與加工品質的一部分，性能還取決於配方、老化及焊接相容性。","捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點","焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合"],"optionsEn":["Thickness contributes to puncture resistance and quality, while formulation, ageing and weld compatibility also matter.","Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored","A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width"],"answer":0,"explanation":"膜厚是耐穿刺與加工品質的一部分，性能還取決於配方、老化及焊接相容性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Thickness contributes to puncture resistance and quality, while formulation, ageing and weld compatibility also matter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b157-v14-10","title":"膜材厚度與批次差異：定量估算","titleEn":"Membrane thickness and batch differences: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「膜材厚度與批次差異」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Membrane thickness and batch differences” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「膜材厚度與批次差異」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Membrane thickness and batch differences\", which statement holds?","options":["圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離","原創教學假設：thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80。","焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面"],"optionsEn":["Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place","Original teaching assumptions: thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80.","After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: thicknessRatio=minimum/nominal=1.6 mm/2.0 mm=0.80. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b157-v14-11","title":"膜材厚度與批次差異：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Membrane thickness and batch differences: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「膜材厚度與批次差異」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Membrane thickness and batch differences” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「膜材厚度與批次差異」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Membrane thickness and batch differences\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容","分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials","Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b157-v14-12","title":"膜材厚度與批次差異：失效診斷","titleEn":"Membrane thickness and batch differences: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「膜材厚度與批次差異」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Membrane thickness and batch differences” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置；若出現局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If a locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到分區量測厚度並追溯捲材批號、接縫和摺痕位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"A locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to map thickness by roll batch, seam and fold position to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膜材厚度與批次差異」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Membrane thickness and batch differences\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合"],"optionsEn":["A locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部薄點在後續施工受壓破裂，平均報告未能預警。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A locally thin point tears under later construction pressure despite a passing average report. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b157-v14-13","title":"焊縫有效寬度與剝離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective seam width and peeling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective seam width and peeling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"焊縫需要連續熔合，外觀寬度不等於有效黏合寬度，污染或皺摺可能形成未熔合通道。剝離與剪切試驗檢查不同受力方式，單一峰值需搭配破壞位置；以完整材料撕裂還是界面分離，會導出不同品質判讀。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度；若出現表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A seam needs continuous fusion; visible width differs from effective bonded width when contamination or folds create channels. Peel and shear test different loading modes. Interpret peak force together with whether failure tears parent material or separates the interface. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width. If surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective seam width and peeling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective seam width and peeling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-13-k1","title":"焊縫有效寬度與剝離","titleEn":"Effective seam width and peeling","text":"焊縫需要連續熔合，外觀寬度不等於有效黏合寬度，污染或皺摺可能形成未熔合通道。剝離與剪切試驗檢查不同受力方式，單一峰值需搭配破壞位置；以完整材料撕裂還是界面分離，會導出不同品質判讀。","textEn":"A seam needs continuous fusion; visible width differs from effective bonded width when contamination or folds create channels. Peel and shear test different loading modes.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective seam width and peeling\" is correct?","options":["焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合","焊縫需要連續熔合，外觀寬度不等於有效黏合寬度，污染或皺摺可能形成未熔合通道。","任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞"],"optionsEn":["A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width","A seam needs continuous fusion; visible width differs from effective bonded width when contamination or folds create channels.","Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane"],"answer":1,"explanation":"焊縫需要連續熔合，外觀寬度不等於有效黏合寬度，污染或皺摺可能形成未熔合通道。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A seam needs continuous fusion; visible width differs from effective bonded width when contamination or folds create channels. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b157-v14-14","title":"焊縫有效寬度與剝離：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective seam width and peeling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective seam width and peeling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective seam width and peeling\", which statement holds?","options":["材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移","內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置","原創教學假設：lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm。"],"optionsEn":["Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail","An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage","Original teaching assumptions: lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: lineResistance=F/width=300 N/50 mm=6 N/mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b157-v14-15","title":"焊縫有效寬度與剝離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective seam width and peeling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective seam width and peeling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective seam width and peeling\"?","options":["將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌"],"optionsEn":["Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b157-v14-16","title":"焊縫有效寬度與剝離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective seam width and peeling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective seam width and peeling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度；若出現表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將剝離與剪切結果配對焊縫破壞面及有效寬度，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to pair peel and shear results with failure faces and effective seam width to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊縫有效寬度與剝離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective seam width and peeling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流。","任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam.","Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane"],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面封口掩蓋內部未熔合通道，水沿接縫串流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Surface closure conceals an unfused internal channel that carries water along the seam. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b157-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」與「分區止水與水路隔離」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects\" and \"Compartments and hydraulic isolation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b157-v14-17","title":"雙焊道試驗與溫度修正：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dual-seam tests and temperature effects” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙焊道中間的封閉通道可提供連續性檢核，但氣壓隨溫度改變，壓降不全代表漏氣。測試區段端部封閉與儀器接頭也可能洩漏，必須與焊縫本體分開；使用絕對壓力與絕對溫度才能作理想氣體比較。 判別這個機制時，應觀察同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果；若出現冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A closed channel between dual seams tests continuity, but pressure varies with temperature and not every drop is leakage. End closures and instrument fittings can leak separately from the seam. Ideal-gas comparison requires absolute pressure and absolute temperature rather than gauge values alone. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together. If cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dual-seam tests and temperature effects” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dual-seam tests and temperature effects”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-17-k1","title":"雙焊道試驗與溫度修正","titleEn":"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects","text":"雙焊道中間的封閉通道可提供連續性檢核，但氣壓隨溫度改變，壓降不全代表漏氣。測試區段端部封閉與儀器接頭也可能洩漏，必須與焊縫本體分開；使用絕對壓力與絕對溫度才能作理想氣體比較。","textEn":"A closed channel between dual seams tests continuity, but pressure varies with temperature and not every drop is leakage. End closures and instrument fittings can leak separately from the seam.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects\" is correct?","options":["任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞","圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離","雙焊道中間的封閉通道可提供連續性檢核，但氣壓隨溫度改變，壓降不全代表漏氣。"],"optionsEn":["Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane","Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place","A closed channel between dual seams tests continuity, but pressure varies with temperature and not every drop is leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙焊道中間的封閉通道可提供連續性檢核，但氣壓隨溫度改變，壓降不全代表漏氣。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A closed channel between dual seams tests continuity, but pressure varies with temperature and not every drop is leakage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b157-v14-18","title":"雙焊道試驗與溫度修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dual-seam tests and temperature effects” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute。","焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面","短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute.","After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check","Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: P2=P1*T2/T1=300 kPa absolute*288 K/293 K=294.9 kPa absolute. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b157-v14-19","title":"雙焊道試驗與溫度修正：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dual-seam tests and temperature effects” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果。","膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together.","High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b157-v14-20","title":"雙焊道試驗與溫度修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dual-seam tests and temperature effects” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果；若出現冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到同步記錄通道絕對壓力、溫度及端封接頭檢漏結果，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to record absolute channel pressure, temperature and end-fitting leak checks together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙焊道試驗與溫度修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dual-seam tests and temperature effects\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離","冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place","Cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding."],"answer":2,"explanation":"冷卻造成壓降被誤判為焊縫漏氣，引出無效重焊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cooling-induced pressure loss is mistaken for a leaking seam and prompts ineffective rewelding. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b157-v14-21","title":"分區止水與水路隔離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Compartments and hydraulic isolation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「分區止水與水路隔離」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compartments and hydraulic isolation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分區系統限制漏水在膜後蔓延，水擋、接頭與後續修復管路必須構成連續邊界。圖上分區不等於實體隔離，跨區穿孔或未連接止水帶可讓一處破損影響很大範圍；驗證要追蹤水路而不只是統計隔板數。 判別這個機制時，應觀察逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口；若出現一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分區止水與水路隔離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compartments limit migration behind the membrane through continuous waterstops, joints and repair interfaces. Drawn zones are not physical isolation: penetrations or disconnected stops can spread one defect widely. Verification therefore traces hydraulic paths rather than counting compartment boundaries. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment. If one cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Compartments and hydraulic isolation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation.","failure":"常見誤解：「圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分區止水與水路隔離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Compartments and hydraulic isolation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-21-k1","title":"分區止水與水路隔離","titleEn":"Compartments and hydraulic isolation","text":"分區系統限制漏水在膜後蔓延，水擋、接頭與後續修復管路必須構成連續邊界。圖上分區不等於實體隔離，跨區穿孔或未連接止水帶可讓一處破損影響很大範圍；驗證要追蹤水路而不只是統計隔板數。","textEn":"Compartments limit migration behind the membrane through continuous waterstops, joints and repair interfaces. Drawn zones are not physical isolation: penetrations or disconnected stops can spread one defect widely.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分區止水與水路隔離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compartments and hydraulic isolation\" is correct?","options":["分區系統限制漏水在膜後蔓延，水擋、接頭與後續修復管路必須構成連續邊界。","圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離","材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移"],"optionsEn":["Compartments limit migration behind the membrane through continuous waterstops, joints and repair interfaces.","Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place","Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail"],"answer":0,"explanation":"分區系統限制漏水在膜後蔓延，水擋、接頭與後續修復管路必須構成連續邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compartments limit migration behind the membrane through continuous waterstops, joints and repair interfaces. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b157-v14-22","title":"分區止水與水路隔離：定量估算","titleEn":"Compartments and hydraulic isolation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分區止水與水路隔離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compartments and hydraulic isolation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分區止水與水路隔離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compartments and hydraulic isolation\", which statement holds?","options":["內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置","原創教學假設：affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation。","只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌"],"optionsEn":["An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage","Original teaching assumptions: affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation.","A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: affectedAreaRatio=oneZone/wholeArea=100 m2/1000 m2=0.10, assuming intact isolation. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b157-v14-23","title":"分區止水與水路隔離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compartments and hydraulic isolation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分區止水與水路隔離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compartments and hydraulic isolation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: One cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If one cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: One cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If one cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分區止水與水路隔離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compartments and hydraulic isolation\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點","逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored","Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b157-v14-24","title":"分區止水與水路隔離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compartments and hydraulic isolation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分區止水與水路隔離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compartments and hydraulic isolation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口；若出現一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If one cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐一核對分區水擋交會、穿透細部及可追溯測試端口，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"One cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit waterstop intersections, penetrations and traceable test ports by compartment to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分區止水與水路隔離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compartments and hydraulic isolation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移"],"optionsEn":["One cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail"],"answer":0,"explanation":"一處跨區缺口讓多區連通，局部維修失去定位能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One cross-zone gap connects compartments and defeats localization of repair. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b157-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「穿透構件與接縫變形」與「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Penetrations and joint movement\" and \"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b157-v14-25","title":"穿透構件與接縫變形：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Penetrations and joint movement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「穿透構件與接縫變形」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Penetrations and joint movement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"支架、預埋件和施工接縫會中斷連續膜面，局部位移常集中在固定點附近。密封細部需要同時容許預期移動並保持水路連續，不能把材料拉伸率直接當作接頭允許位移；自由長度、固定方式及多方向變形都要確認。 判別這個機制時，應觀察比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形；若出現固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「穿透構件與接縫變形」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Brackets, embedded items and joints interrupt membrane continuity and concentrate movement near fixings. Details must accommodate movement while preserving water isolation. Material elongation is not the joint movement allowance: free length, restraint and multidirectional deformation require separate verification. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response. If fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Penetrations and joint movement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「穿透構件與接縫變形」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Penetrations and joint movement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-25-k1","title":"穿透構件與接縫變形","titleEn":"Penetrations and joint movement","text":"支架、預埋件和施工接縫會中斷連續膜面，局部位移常集中在固定點附近。密封細部需要同時容許預期移動並保持水路連續，不能把材料拉伸率直接當作接頭允許位移；自由長度、固定方式及多方向變形都要確認。","textEn":"Brackets, embedded items and joints interrupt membrane continuity and concentrate movement near fixings. Details must accommodate movement while preserving water isolation.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「穿透構件與接縫變形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Penetrations and joint movement\" is correct?","options":["材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移","支架、預埋件和施工接縫會中斷連續膜面，局部位移常集中在固定點附近。","焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面"],"optionsEn":["Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail","Brackets, embedded items and joints interrupt membrane continuity and concentrate movement near fixings.","After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check"],"answer":1,"explanation":"支架、預埋件和施工接縫會中斷連續膜面，局部位移常集中在固定點附近。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Brackets, embedded items and joints interrupt membrane continuity and concentrate movement near fixings. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b157-v14-26","title":"穿透構件與接縫變形：定量估算","titleEn":"Penetrations and joint movement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「穿透構件與接縫變形」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Penetrations and joint movement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「穿透構件與接縫變形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Penetrations and joint movement\", which statement holds?","options":["短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容","膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面","原創教學假設：nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。"],"optionsEn":["Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials","High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections","Original teaching assumptions: nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: nominalStrain=movement/freeLength=5 mm/100 mm=0.05=5 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b157-v14-27","title":"穿透構件與接縫變形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Penetrations and joint movement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「穿透構件與接縫變形」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Penetrations and joint movement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「穿透構件與接縫變形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Penetrations and joint movement\"?","options":["比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合"],"optionsEn":["Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b157-v14-28","title":"穿透構件與接縫變形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Penetrations and joint movement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「穿透構件與接縫變形」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Penetrations and joint movement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形；若出現固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比較接頭位移方向、膜材自由長度及穿透處試件變形，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare joint movement directions, membrane free length and penetration-specimen response to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「穿透構件與接縫變形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Penetrations and joint movement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂。","焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing.","After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check"],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定點太靠近接縫使小位移集中成撕裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fixings too close to a joint concentrate small movement into tearing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b157-v14-29","title":"隱蔽前損傷與後續工序：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"焊縫檢驗後的膜材仍可能被鋼筋、墊塊或台車碰傷，檢查時間因而決定證據有效範圍。修補片會新增邊界與搭接，必須索引到原缺陷位置；最後隱蔽前檢查應覆蓋後續施工造成的損傷，而非重複舊報告。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結；若出現檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Membranes can be damaged by reinforcement, spacers or carriages after seam testing, so inspection timing defines evidence validity. Patches add new boundaries and overlaps and must trace back to defects. Final pre-cover inspection must address damage from subsequent work rather than merely repeat an earlier report. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade. If reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-29-k1","title":"隱蔽前損傷與後續工序","titleEn":"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work","text":"焊縫檢驗後的膜材仍可能被鋼筋、墊塊或台車碰傷，檢查時間因而決定證據有效範圍。修補片會新增邊界與搭接，必須索引到原缺陷位置；最後隱蔽前檢查應覆蓋後續施工造成的損傷，而非重複舊報告。","textEn":"Membranes can be damaged by reinforcement, spacers or carriages after seam testing, so inspection timing defines evidence validity. Patches add new boundaries and overlaps and must trace back to defects.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work\" is correct?","options":["焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面","內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置","焊縫檢驗後的膜材仍可能被鋼筋、墊塊或台車碰傷，檢查時間因而決定證據有效範圍。"],"optionsEn":["After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check","An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage","Membranes can be damaged by reinforcement, spacers or carriages after seam testing, so inspection timing defines evidence validity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"焊縫檢驗後的膜材仍可能被鋼筋、墊塊或台車碰傷，檢查時間因而決定證據有效範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Membranes can be damaged by reinforcement, spacers or carriages after seam testing, so inspection timing defines evidence validity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b157-v14-30","title":"隱蔽前損傷與後續工序：定量估算","titleEn":"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent。","只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌","捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent.","A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining","Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: recheckCoverage=areasAfterLastTrade/totalAreas=18/20=90 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b157-v14-31","title":"隱蔽前損傷與後續工序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結。","任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade.","Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b157-v14-32","title":"隱蔽前損傷與後續工序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結；若出現檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「焊接檢驗完成後就永遠不需再次查看膜面」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"After seam inspection the membrane surface never needs another check\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將膜材照片、修補編號與最後一道交叉工序完成時間連結，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to link membrane photographs and patch IDs to completion of the final crossing trade to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隱蔽前損傷與後續工序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pre-concealment damage and subsequent work\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置","檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage","Reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record."],"answer":2,"explanation":"檢驗後被鋼筋刺穿，舊合格紀錄無法代表隱蔽時狀態。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reinforcement punctures a previously tested membrane and invalidates its earlier passing record. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b157-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「漏水定位與表面假象」與「耐久相容與維護交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Leak localization and surface symptoms\" and \"Durability compatibility and handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b157-v14-33","title":"漏水定位與表面假象：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Leak localization and surface symptoms: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「漏水定位與表面假象」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Leak localization and surface symptoms” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"隧道內出水位置未必位於膜材破損處，水可能沿膜後、接縫或空腔移動。只封住可見出口會改變水路，甚至提高局部壓力；診斷需整合分區圖、排水量及時間變化，區分新缺陷、既有連通與排水阻塞。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖；若出現出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漏水定位與表面假象」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The interior discharge location need not coincide with membrane damage because water migrates behind layers and through joints or cavities. Sealing an outlet redirects paths and may raise local pressure. Combine compartment maps, flow and timing to distinguish new damage, connectivity and blocked drains. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together. If a sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Leak localization and surface symptoms” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min.","failure":"常見誤解：「內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漏水定位與表面假象」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Leak localization and surface symptoms”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-33-k1","title":"漏水定位與表面假象","titleEn":"Leak localization and surface symptoms","text":"隧道內出水位置未必位於膜材破損處，水可能沿膜後、接縫或空腔移動。只封住可見出口會改變水路，甚至提高局部壓力；診斷需整合分區圖、排水量及時間變化，區分新缺陷、既有連通與排水阻塞。","textEn":"The interior discharge location need not coincide with membrane damage because water migrates behind layers and through joints or cavities. Sealing an outlet redirects paths and may raise local pressure.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漏水定位與表面假象」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Leak localization and surface symptoms\" is correct?","options":["隧道內出水位置未必位於膜材破損處，水可能沿膜後、接縫或空腔移動。","內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置","短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容"],"optionsEn":["The interior discharge location need not coincide with membrane damage because water migrates behind layers and through joints or cavities.","An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage","Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials"],"answer":0,"explanation":"隧道內出水位置未必位於膜材破損處，水可能沿膜後、接縫或空腔移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The interior discharge location need not coincide with membrane damage because water migrates behind layers and through joints or cavities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b157-v14-34","title":"漏水定位與表面假象：定量估算","titleEn":"Leak localization and surface symptoms: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漏水定位與表面假象」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Leak localization and surface symptoms” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漏水定位與表面假象」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Leak localization and surface symptoms\", which statement holds?","options":["膜材延伸率高就能容許任意尖突基面","原創教學假設：leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min。","焊縫外觀平滑就能證明全寬熔合"],"optionsEn":["High membrane elongation permits a substrate with any sharp projections","Original teaching assumptions: leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min.","A smooth seam appearance proves fusion across its entire width"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: leakRate=collectedVolume/time=6 L/20 min=0.30 L/min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b157-v14-35","title":"漏水定位與表面假象：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Leak localization and surface symptoms: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漏水定位與表面假象」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Leak localization and surface symptoms” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漏水定位與表面假象」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Leak localization and surface symptoms\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","圖紙畫成多個分區就能保證實際水路隔離","將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Multiple compartments drawn on a plan guarantee hydraulic isolation in place","Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b157-v14-36","title":"漏水定位與表面假象：失效診斷","titleEn":"Leak localization and surface symptoms: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漏水定位與表面假象」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Leak localization and surface symptoms” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖；若出現出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If a sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「內表面漏水位置一定就是膜材破損的位置」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An interior leak always marks the exact location of membrane damage\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將出水位置、分區端口反應與水位變化共同繪圖，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"A sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to map discharge, compartment-port responses and groundwater changes together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漏水定位與表面假象」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Leak localization and surface symptoms\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容"],"optionsEn":["A sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials"],"answer":0,"explanation":"出口被封後轉移到鄰區，原來的膜破損仍未修復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A sealed outlet moves to a neighbouring area while the original membrane defect remains. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b157-v14-37","title":"耐久相容與維護交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Durability compatibility and handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「耐久相容與維護交接」如何影響隧道防水膜鋪設的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Durability compatibility and handover” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tunnel waterproofing-membrane installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"防水膜與修補材料的相容性可能受塑化劑、溫度和地下水化學影響，短期黏著良好不能保證長期功能。交接應保存原材料、焊接及分區資料，讓未來修繕能確認材料搭配；未知材料直接覆貼可能使原系統更難診斷。 判別這個機制時，應觀察核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷；若出現失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「耐久相容與維護交接」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compatibility with repair materials can depend on plasticizers, temperature and groundwater chemistry; initial adhesion does not establish durability. Retain material, welding and compartment records for future selection. Overlaying unknown materials can make the original system harder to diagnose and maintain. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories. If lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Durability compatibility and handover” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「耐久相容與維護交接」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Durability compatibility and handover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-37-k1","title":"耐久相容與維護交接","titleEn":"Durability compatibility and handover","text":"防水膜與修補材料的相容性可能受塑化劑、溫度和地下水化學影響，短期黏著良好不能保證長期功能。交接應保存原材料、焊接及分區資料，讓未來修繕能確認材料搭配；未知材料直接覆貼可能使原系統更難診斷。","textEn":"Compatibility with repair materials can depend on plasticizers, temperature and groundwater chemistry; initial adhesion does not establish durability. Retain material, welding and compartment records for future selection.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「耐久相容與維護交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Durability compatibility and handover\" is correct?","options":["短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容","防水膜與修補材料的相容性可能受塑化劑、溫度和地下水化學影響，短期黏著良好不能保證長期功能。","只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌"],"optionsEn":["Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials","Compatibility with repair materials can depend on plasticizers, temperature and groundwater chemistry; initial adhesion does not establish durability.","A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining"],"answer":1,"explanation":"防水膜與修補材料的相容性可能受塑化劑、溫度和地下水化學影響，短期黏著良好不能保證長期功能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compatibility with repair materials can depend on plasticizers, temperature and groundwater chemistry; initial adhesion does not establish durability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b157-v14-38","title":"耐久相容與維護交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Durability compatibility and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「耐久相容與維護交接」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Durability compatibility and handover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent。防水膜阻隔滲水，承壓與排水責任仍須由整體襯砌系統承擔。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent. The membrane blocks seepage, while the lining system must carry pressure or provide drainage. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「耐久相容與維護交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Durability compatibility and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["捲材平均厚度合格就能忽略局部薄點","任何試壓壓降都能直接證明膜材有破洞","原創教學假設：recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent。"],"optionsEn":["Passing mean roll thickness permits local thin points to be ignored","Every pressure-test drop directly proves a hole in the membrane","Original teaching assumptions: recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: recordCompleteness=linkedRolls/installedRolls=48/50=96 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b157-v14-39","title":"耐久相容與維護交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Durability compatibility and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「耐久相容與維護交接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Durability compatibility and handover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「耐久相容與維護交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Durability compatibility and handover\"?","options":["核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","材料斷裂延伸率就是所有穿透細部的允許位移"],"optionsEn":["Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Material break elongation is the allowable movement of every penetration detail"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b157-v14-40","title":"耐久相容與維護交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Durability compatibility and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"prerequisiteIds":["b157-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「耐久相容與維護交接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Durability compatibility and handover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷；若出現失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「短期貼得牢就代表修補材料能長期相容」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Strong initial adhesion proves long-term compatibility of repair materials\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b157-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到核對材料批次、相容性證據、分區圖與修補履歷，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit batches, compatibility evidence, compartment maps and patch histories to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]},{"id":"b157-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「耐久相容與維護交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Durability compatibility and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏。","只要有防水膜地下水壓就不會作用在襯砌"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage.","A waterproof membrane prevents groundwater pressure from acting on the lining"],"answer":1,"explanation":"失去材料身分後採不相容修補，造成界面劣化和再漏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Lost material identity leads to incompatible repair, interface degradation and renewed leakage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel","v14s-sika-membrane"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
